  "kashmir-tour-packages-from-nepal": {
    sections: [
      { h: "Flights and airlines from Kathmandu", p: ["Nepal Airlines, Air India, IndiGo and other carriers fly between Kathmandu and Delhi, with onward flights to Srinagar. Overland, border crossings such as Sunauli and Raxaul connect to Indian railway stations.", "India is 15 minutes behind Nepal."] },
      { h: "Power, money and practical tips for Nepali travellers", p: ["India and Nepal both use 230-volt power with similar round-pin plugs (types C, D and M), so most Nepali devices work without an adapter.", "Indian rupees are needed in Kashmir; Nepali rupees are not accepted. Change money before you travel or withdraw from ATMs in India. Cards and UPI work in larger shops and hotels where your bank supports them."] },
      { h: "Kashmir's weather compared with Nepal", p: ["Nepali travellers used to the hills will find Kashmir's seasons familiar, but the valley is drier and its winter snow more reliable in Gulmarg. Summer is pleasant and green, and autumn is clear and golden, much like the Kathmandu valley after the monsoon."] },
      { h: "How Nepali travellers usually plan Kashmir", p: ["Nepali visitors often spend 6 to 8 nights, sometimes combining Kashmir with Vaishno Devi, Amritsar or Delhi. Autumn, around the Dashain and Tihar holidays, is a popular time."] },
      { h: "Kashmir for families from Nepal", p: ["Nepali families travelling with elderly parents should plan the long road or rail journey in comfortable stages, with a night in Delhi or Jammu on the way, and choose hotels with lifts and vegetarian meals."] },
      { h: "Kashmir honeymoon from Nepal", p: ["Nepali honeymooners often choose Kashmir for its lakes and houseboats, which are very different from Nepal's mountains. A Deluxe houseboat, Gulmarg and Pahalgam make a classic week."] },
      { h: "Shopping in Kashmir and taking it home to Nepal", p: ["Saffron, dry fruit, shawls and papier mache are popular gifts. Check customs rules on returning to Nepal for high-value items, and keep receipts."] },
      { h: "Adding Ladakh to a trip from Nepal", p: ["Nepali citizens should check current permit rules for Ladakh's protected areas before planning; requirements can differ from those for other foreign nationals."] },
      { h: "Visa application step by step for travellers from Nepal", p: ["Nepali citizens do not need a visa for India. For flights, carry a valid passport, which is the simplest accepted document; airlines and airport security may also accept certain other government photo IDs, but rules can change, so check with your airline. Keep photocopies for hotels and checkpoints. Children should carry their own identity documents or birth certificates as required by the airline.", "If you are travelling overland, keep your ID ready at the border crossing and on trains, and carry printed copies of hotel bookings."] },
      { h: "Combining Kashmir with Vaishno Devi and Amritsar from Nepal", p: ["Many Nepali visitors combine Kashmir with pilgrim and heritage stops in North India. A popular plan is Delhi, then a train to Amritsar for the Golden Temple and the Wagah border ceremony, onward to Katra for Vaishno Devi, and the Vande Bharat to Srinagar for five or six days in Kashmir, flying back to Delhi and Kathmandu at the end."] },
      { h: "An 8-day Kashmir plan for travellers from Nepal", p: ["Day 1: fly Kathmandu to Delhi and on to Srinagar. Day 2: Srinagar. Day 3: Gulmarg. Day 4: Sonamarg. Day 5 and 6: Pahalgam. Day 7: Srinagar temples, including Shankaracharya and Kheer Bhawani. Day 8: fly home."] },
      { h: "Nepali holidays and the best time to go", p: ["Many Nepali visitors travel during Dashain and Tihar in October and November, when Kashmir's chinars turn golden and skies are clear. Spring, around the Nepali new year in April, brings tulips and blossom. Winter suits those who want snow."] },
      { h: "Getting around Kashmir as a visitor from Nepal", p: ["Nepali visitors get around like Indian travellers: a private car with driver is easiest, with union taxis in Pahalgam and Sonamarg and shikaras on the lakes. Carry your passport or accepted ID at all times for hotels and checkpoints. Hindi is widely understood, which makes travel easy for most Nepali visitors."] },
      { h: "Health, insurance and medical facilities", p: ["Travel insurance that explicitly covers Jammu and Kashmir, and Ladakh if you go there, is strongly advised, because some policies exclude regions under travel advisories. Srinagar has major hospitals, and towns have clinics and pharmacies; remote areas such as Gurez and the high passes have limited facilities. Carry any regular medicines with prescriptions, a basic first-aid kit and, for Ladakh, any altitude medication your doctor recommends. Drink bottled or filtered water, and in winter keep warm to avoid colds."] },
      { h: "Where international travellers like to stay", p: ["International visitors often prefer a Deluxe houseboat for one or two nights, a centrally heated international-brand or heritage hotel in Srinagar, a resort near the Gondola in Gulmarg and a riverside hotel in Pahalgam. Ask for hotels experienced with foreign guests: they handle Form C registration smoothly and understand dietary needs. In winter, confirm heating in every hotel and houseboat."] },
    ],
    faqs: [
      { q: "What is the time difference between Nepal and India?", a: "India is 15 minutes behind Nepal." },
      { q: "Do I need a plug adapter in Kashmir if I travel from Nepal?", a: "India and Nepal both use 230-volt power with similar round-pin plugs (types C, D and M), so most Nepali devices work without an adapter." },
      { q: "How many days do I need for Kashmir from Nepal?", a: "Six to eight days for Srinagar, Gulmarg, Sonamarg and Pahalgam, plus travel time and a buffer before your flight home." },
      { q: "Is English spoken in Kashmir?", a: "Yes, widely in hotels, by drivers and in tourist areas, along with Hindi, Urdu and Kashmiri." },
      { q: "Do I need travel insurance for Kashmir?", a: "It is strongly advised. Make sure the policy explicitly covers Jammu and Kashmir, and Ladakh if you go there." },
    ],
  },
